          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.112,
            0.709,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Construct triangles for the following measurements:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.136,
            0.392,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) 75°, 5 cm, 75°"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.159,
            0.393,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) 25°, 3 cm, 60°"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.184,
            0.403,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) 120°, 6 cm, 30°"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.214,
            0.43,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do triangles always exist?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.238,
            0.813,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Do triangles exist for every combination of two angles and their included side? Explore."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.829,
            0.226,
            0.917,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.829,
                0.226,
                0.917,
                0.278
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.276,
            0.849,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As in the case when we are given all three sides, it turns out that there is not always a triangle for every combination of two angles and the included side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.34,
            0.848,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find examples of measurements of two angles with the included side where a triangle is not possible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.39,
            0.848,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us try to visualise such a situation. Once the base is drawn, try to imagine how the other sides should be so that they do not meet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.428,
            0.514,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here are some obvious examples."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.451,
            0.792,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.204,
                0.451,
                0.792,
                0.525
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.537,
            0.847,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the two angles are greater than or equal to a right angle (90°), then it is clear that a triangle is not possible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.575,
            0.848,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now we make one of the base angles an acute angle, say "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What are the possible values that the other angle should take so that the lines don’t meet?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.375,
            0.633,
            0.622,
            0.766
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.375,
                0.633,
                0.622,
                0.766
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_16.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.782,
            0.846,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? It is clear that if the line from B is “inclined” sufficiently to the right, then it will not meet the line l."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.837,
            0.847,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) Try to find a possible ∠B (marked in the figure) for this to happen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
